# What the run guarantees: CUDA hidden, the CPU lease held, the staging set installed only when each prompt's manifest
# carries its `# complete` trailer.
kind: exclusive
reason: musespark_dump runs mainline llama.cpp on 32 CPU threads over a 225 GB mmap; beside a timed run or a gate batch
  it would take their cores and their page cache, so it holds the lease; why now: the real tier's oracle sets the Muse
